{
  "rules": [
    "Strong positive bias: forecasts are consistently too high vs realized prices, especially beyond ~day 10; apply a downward level shift that increases with horizon.",
    "Regime-change blindness: when the recent history is flat-to-down, the model still projects stable-to-rising prices; add a trend filter so negative momentum forces a lower path.",
    "Overshoot after local highs/spikes: following a jump in the last observed days, the model extrapolates strength, but outcomes mean-revert and then sell off; dampen post-spike projections and enforce mean reversion toward the recent 20–30d average.",
    "Horizon-dependent divergence: early horizon (days 1–5) errors are small, but mid/late horizon (days 10–30) errors grow rapidly; use a widening correction (e.g., subtract an increasing penalty per forecast day).",
    "Volatility underestimation on the downside: realized paths show sharp drawdowns that the model misses; incorporate a downside stress adjustment when recent volatility is elevated or when price breaks below recent support (e.g., 10–15d low)."
  ]
}
